    "text": "User Datagram Protocol (UDP) > UDP is aconnectionless, unreliable transport protocol. > It does not add anything to the services of IP except to provide process-to process communication. > Performs very limited error checking. Why UDP? > SDP IS a simple protocol using a minimum of overhead. > Aa process wants to send a small message and does not care much about reliability, it can use UDP. > Sénding a small message by using UDP takes much less interaction between the sender and receiver than using TCP.",
